<code>assert \result != -1 => \forall int i; \result < i && i < this.size(); (this.get(i) == null) == (o == null) && (o != null => !o.equals(this.get(i)));</code>

This assert statement ensures that if the result of `lastIndexOf` is not `-1`, then for every index `i` greater than the result and less than the size of the list, the element at that index is either `null` (if the searched object `o` is `null`) or not equal to the searched object `o` (if `o` is not `null`).
